        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_team_folders" />
        <field name="name">Common problems</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">61</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <div class="table-responsive"><table class="table table-sm table-bordered"><thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>What it means</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>No Team Folders menu after installing</td><td>Your window has the old menu</td><td>Reload Odoo, or close and reopen the installed app</td></tr><tr><td>Required fields are empty, with Content in red</td><td>You're on the form for a new file, not a folder</td><td>Discard it, then go to Team Folders › New</td></tr><tr><td>No New button under Team Folders</td><td>You aren't a Team Folder Manager</td><td>Ask an administrator</td></tr><tr><td>A team folder isn't listed</td><td>You aren't on that folder</td><td>Ask a manager to add you</td></tr><tr><td>The document opens read-only</td><td>You're a Viewer of that folder</td><td>Ask a manager to make you a Member</td></tr><tr><td>No Open in ONLYOFFICE button</td><td>The file is in a plain folder, or it's a file type ONLYOFFICE can't open</td><td>Move it to a team folder, or check the file type</td></tr><tr><td>ONLYOFFICE can't be reached</td><td>The Docs server is down, or its address changed</td><td>Ask an administrator to check the ONLYOFFICE settings</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

